  "responsibility": "One workhorse for each checkout of a tab session: its starter, queue, operations and board news, built on first use",
  "description": "A workhorse works in its checkout, the directory that holds its vault, and its thread-link key is the tab session and the checkout together. It belongs to the checkout, not to the repository identity, so a new chosen checkout leaves it linked. A stop for one checkout interrupts the turn that workhorse runs, and a stop for the tab interrupts the turn of every workhorse. The coordinator's stop_workhorses tool stops every running workhorse of the tab by voice.",
